---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import NextStep from '../components/NextStep.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base
  title="The House"
  description="The history of TrailSide Events PA: mill, lumber yard, Lehigh Stove Co., Insurrection Distillery, and the house Jordan and Brandon Cummins opened in Lehighton in 2024."
>
  <article class="page">
    <header class="wrap mast">
      <p class="eyebrow">The house</p>
      <h1>A mill building that learned how to host.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        {site.owners} opened TrailSide in spring 2024 at {site.address.line}, across from Dunbar Bottling Co. and beside the D&amp;L Trail. They describe it as a historic performance and event venue with rustic elegance and modern amenities.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="wrap split">
      <blockquote class="quote" data-reveal>
        <p>“We couldn’t shake our love for this space.”</p>
        <footer>Jordan Cummins, to Times News, May 2, 2024. She and Brandon had first pictured a bar and restaurant, then shaped an event house around the rest of their lives.</footer>
      </blockquote>
      <div data-reveal>
        <p>
          In that same interview, Jordan said the area had few rooms for special occasions. TrailSide would rent the space, host its own events, and collaborate with Half Barrel Brewing and other local businesses for community gatherings.
        </p>
        <p>
          The name TrailSide Events was inspired by the building’s place next to the historic D&amp;L Trail. The Lehigh Stove Co. years are honored with an original stove still in the house.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="section-kicker">On the record</p>
        <h2 class="section-title">How the building arrived here</h2>
        <ol class="chapter-list">
          <li data-reveal>
            <span class="when">1865</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Lehigh Stove Co.</h3>
              <p>The building at 201 North Main Lane dates to 1865 and first housed Lehigh Stove and Manufacturing. An original stove from that work is still in the room.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li data-reveal>
            <span class="when">The Flats</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Henry Miller Planing Mill</h3>
              <p>Henry Miller’s planing mill stood on the Flats and employed about ten people. After his death, his sons kept the shop as Miller Brothers.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li data-reveal>
            <span class="when">1930s</span>
            <div>
              <h3>City Lumber Company</h3>
              <p>City Lumber Company succeeded the mill operation in the 1930s.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li data-reveal>
            <span class="when">2019–2023</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Insurrection Distillery</h3>
              <p>Rod Walck and Anthony Serafino opened a grain-to-glass distillery here in fall 2019, with a soft opening on October 26. They made bourbon, vodka, rum, moonshine, and rye until it closed in April 2023.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li data-reveal>
            <span class="when">May 2, 2024</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Ribbon cutting</h3>
              <p>6–8 p.m. with the Carbon County Chamber. Bookings opened after that evening.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li data-reveal>
            <span class="when">Nov 14, 2025</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Business of the Year</h3>
              <p>Carbon County Chamber &amp; Economic Development Corporation, at the chamber’s Annual Awards Gala.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol>
        <NextStep title="See what the house is for." copy="Weddings, showers, birthdays, performances, and the practical things already in the room." href="/gatherings" label="Gatherings" />
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>
